<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">County of Pallars Sobirà</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1011–<a href="/years/1487">1487</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The County of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pallars">Pallars</a> Sobirà was the upper, northern half of the Pyrenean county of Pallars, centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sort">Sort</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valls-daneu">Àneu valleys</a>, created in the division of 1011. Its counts became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> and Aragon but kept wide local powers, and it was the last Catalan county to be extinguished, confiscated by the Crown of Aragon in 1487.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/county-of-pallars-sobira.jpg" alt="County of Pallars Sobirà" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Germenfer · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banner_of_the_Counts_of_Pallars.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
